464 2291 2374 L 2291 2349 Q 2534 2304 2748 2166 Q 2963 2029 3097 1795 Q 3232 1562 3232 1222 Q 3232 838 3043 547 Q 2854 256 2512 89 Q 2170 -77 1715 -77 Q 1331 -77 1059 35 Q 787 147 598 320 Q 410 493 269 685 L 672 992 Q 845 730 1072 566 Q 1299 403 1709 403 Q 2182 403 2425 620 Q 2669 838 2669 1229 L 2669 1280 Q 2669 1677 2425 1891 Q 2182 2106 1709 2106 L 1184 2106 L 1184 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-90\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(213.240156 57.591471) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-8f\" d=\"M 2163 397 L 1677 397 L 1677 1734 L 429 1734 L 429 2170 L 1677 2170 L 1677 3507 L 2163 3507 L 2163 2170 L 3411 2170 L 3411 1734 L 2163 1734 L 2163 397 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" d=\"M 1926 -77 Q 1466 -77 1130 131 Q 794 339 611 723 Q 429 1107 429 1638 Q 429 2138 573 2573 Q 717 3008 957 3373 Q 1197 3738 1475 4016 Q 1754 4294 2022 4467 L 2714 4467 Q 2240 4122 1897 3786 Q 1555 3450 1331 3059 Q 1107 2669 986 2150 L 1018 2138 Q 1126 2323 1270 2467 Q 1414 2611 1619 2694 Q 1824 2778 2093 2778 Q 2477 2778 2774 2611 Q 3072 2445 3241 2134 Q 3411 1824 3411 1402 Q 3411 966 3225 630 Q 3040 294 2707 108 Q 2374 -77 1926 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2214 390 2422 499 Q 2630 608 2742 819 Q 2854 1030 2854 1331 L 2854 1382 Q 2854 1683 2742 1894 Q 2630 2106 2422 2214 Q 2214 2323 1920 2323 Q 1626 2323 1418 2214 Q 1210 2106 1098 1894 Q 986 1683 986 1382 L 986 1331 Q 986 1030 1098 819 Q 1210 608 1418 499 Q 1626 390 1920 390 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-8f\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(323.164832 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" d=\"M 2912 0 L 2400 0 L 2400 877 L 243 877 L 243 1350 L 2112 4467 L 2912 4467 L 2912 1325 L 3558 1325 L 3558 877 L 2912 877 L 2912 0 z\nM 2368 4051 L 749 1325 L 2400 1325 L 2400 4051 L 2368 4051 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-8f\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(180 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(207.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p520c2d5414\"><rect x=\"48.548281\" y=\"11.974471\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Annual operating profit by utilisation ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Profit = 20kt × utilisation × $1,800 − $21M.</p> <ul><li>50%: <b>−$3.0M</b>, payback —</li><li>75%: <b>+$6.0M</b>, payback 15.0 years</li><li>90%: <b>+$11.4M</b>, payback 7.9 years</li></ul> <p>Break-even utilisation: $21M ÷ (20kt × $1,800) = <b>58%</b>.</p> <p>To pay back in eight years the plant must earn $11.25M a year, which needs <b>90% utilisation</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> only near-full running meets the hurdle; at 75% payback takes 15 years, and at 50% the plant loses money.</p>"},{"q":"Only 45% of capacity is contracted. What does that tell you, and what would you do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Contracted volume alone (45%) is below the 58% break-even: the plant would lose money on signed contracts only.</p> <ul><li>Sign more <b>long-term supply contracts</b> with battery factories and carmakers before committing the full $90M</li> <li><b>Build in phases</b>: a first line sized to contracted volume, then expand</li> <li><b>Offer gate-fee discounts</b> for multi-year commitments</li> <li><b>Hedge metal prices</b> partly, since lithium and nickel prices swing sharply</li></ul>"},{"q":"What risks would you raise with the board?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Metal prices: a fall in lithium or nickel cuts the $1,800 margin per tonne</li><li>Battery chemistry: newer batteries use less cobalt and nickel, so they're worth less to recycle</li> <li>Timing: car batteries reach end of life slowly, so the plant depends on factory scrap for years</li><li>Competition for scrap from other European recyclers</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't build the full plant yet. It needs 58% utilisation to break even and about 90% to pay back within eight years, yet only 45% of capacity is under contract; at 75% it would take 15 years to pay back. I recommend building in phases sized to contracted volume and signing long-term supply deals before adding capacity. Risk: metal price swings change the margin per tonne. Next step: approach the three largest battery factories in the Nordics for multi-year supply agreements.","great":["Recognises utilisation drives profit in a fixed-cost plant","Compares contracted volume with break-even","Proposes phasing to reduce risk","Raises metal-price and chemistry risks"],"id":42,"slug":"northcairn-recycling"}